# Smart Habit — Supabase configuration (STEP 1: persistence).
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development and fill in the values
# from your own Supabase project (Project Settings → API). NEVER commit
# a real `.env` file, and NEVER paste real keys into chat, code, or docs
# — keys are supplied via the secure flow only.
# EXPO_PUBLIC variables are inlined at build time: after changing them,
# restart the dev server (`expo start`) or rebuild the app.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# STEP 3: RevenueCat configuration. The value is the Google Play
# public SDK key from the RevenueCat dashboard (Project Settings →
# API keys). NEVER commit a real key, and NEVER paste one into chat,
# code, or docs — keys are supplied via the secure flow only, or as
# EAS secrets for builds. Leave this empty and the app keeps its
# exact preview behaviour (plan names only, no prices, no purchase).
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_API_KEY=
# STEP 5: Firebase configuration. Firebase has NO env var here and NO
# key in this file: Android configuration lives ONLY in
# google-services.json, downloaded from your Firebase console and
# placed at the project root for a dev build. NEVER commit
# google-services.json, NEVER paste its contents into chat, code, or
# docs — it is supplied via the secure flow only. Without it, the app
# keeps its exact unconfigured behaviour (no events are sent).
